  <title id="bdl11onlineselection-title">Online selection of layerwise prior variances with the Laplace marginal likelihood</title>
  <desc id="bdl11onlineselection-desc">Four panels. First, the log Laplace marginal likelihood log q of D given M increases monotonically over training steps in several stages and levels off. Second, the layerwise prior variances change during training: one rises steadily while the others drop and settle. Third and fourth, the predictive class probability over a two-dimensional input space with the training points of two classes shown as dots and crosses: the optimized model has a smooth, gradual decision boundary, while the naively trained model has a sharp, irregular boundary with isolated patches. A grey-scale bar maps shading to probabilities from 0 to 1.</desc>
